game MW
// Longnose Cab tuning (the user, 2026-10-31): "as fast as the raptor and 2x as heavy as the raptor". Weight 14,000 kg
// (the tuned Raptor's 7,000 x 2). The truck takes the tuned Raptor's drivetrain and tyre size (raptor.nfsms v2 values,
// read from the game's database) with every force doubled, so twice the force on twice the weight moves it like the
// Raptor: torque x2, the Raptor's rev range, gears, final gear, differential and torque split (same tyre size, so the
// same speed per rev), the Raptor's grip coefficients (grip scales with the weight on the tyres), brakes and handbrake
// x2, drag and downforce x2; the truck's own turbo zeroed (the Raptor has none). Both stages (stock and _top).
// v2 (the user, after the first race: half the Raptor's acceleration, wheelspin): GRIP_SCALE 2 in both stages, as
// the game's tyre grip did not grow with the doubled weight.
// v3 (the user, 2026-11-01, after screenshots showed the chassis scraping the road): suspension at twice the
// Raptor's in each stage (springs, shock compression and rebound, anti-roll bars); ride height, travel and
// progression stay the mod's. Grip back to 1: x2 did not help (v2), the wheelspin came from the scraping.
// v4 (the user, 2026-11-01: the truck drifts whenever it turns): the tuned Raptor's handling values in each stage,
// so the truck is physically the Raptor at twice the weight and force: tyre STEERING, YAW_SPEED, YAW_CONTROL (the
// truck's stability help was nearly off at speed: 0.1 against 0.95), BRAKE_LOCK (rear 3.5 against 1.7), the
// physics geometry (WHEEL_BASE, TRACK_WIDTH, FRONT_AXLE, FRONT_WEIGHT_BIAS, ROLL_CENTER, AERO_CG), shock valving,
// digression, spring progression, SHOCK_BLOWOUT, and TENSOR_SCALE (2 against 2.87). Ride height and travel stay.
// Generated from the unpacked database; the truck's looks, cameras, suspension and steering stay the mod's.
